{"text": "NANCY GUIDEN\n\nPROFILE: Extensive project management and communications/media experience in the private,\npublic, Federal/DoD workspace, and political sectors. Staff supervisor. Process improvement\nspecialist. Expertise in major event creation and management. Exhibits strong problem solving,\nanalytical, relationship-building, and superior organizational skills. Active TS/SCI clearance.\n\n2 SR a EES\n\nEMPLOYMENT HISTORY\n\nDonald Trump Transition Team, September 2016 \u2014 January 2017\ne Provided support to the Agency Action Team and all 300+ members in order to compile\nindividual plans for all departments and agencies in government to use as a guide for\ngoverning beginning on January 20, 2017\n\nAdvanced Resource Technologies, Inc. (ARTI), 2015-2016\nProgram Analyst (Contractor) for a Department of Defense government client\ne Provided support to the Director & Deputy Director with administrative/program\nanalysis, reporting, and measuring of data/statistics.\n\nBooz Allen Hamilton, Washington, DC, 2008 \u2014 2015\nContractor for a Department of Defense government client\ne Duties included strategic planning, communications strategies, public outreach,\nresponding to Congressional inquiries, and process improvement. Provided\nadministrative/program analysis, reporting, and measuring of data/statistics. Writing and\nediting of newsletters, annual reports & reports to the client. Supervised a staff of four.\n\nOn Sabbatical, 2006-2008, Chicago, IL, Caretaker for immediate family member.\n\nU.S. Environmental Protection Agency, Washington, DC and Chicago, IL\nPolitical Appointee, Senior Project Manager/Public Affairs Liaison, from 2002\u20142006\nFrom 2004\u20142006 (Chicago, IL)\ne Managed communications/media relations for the implementation of a Presidential\nExecutive Order to restore and protect The Great Lakes.\ne Successfully managed a team of EPA senior staff, state and federal officials, and various\nnon-governmental organizations that provided input for the creation of the restoration\nplan.\ne Secured and managed $450K budget, and acted as contract administrator for external\nproject consultants.\nFrom 2002\u20142004 (Washington, DC)\n\u00a9 Served as advisor to the EPA Administrator on external communications efforts, focused\non building and strengthening relationships with the national media. Created a formal\nmedia relations process, which formerly did not exist, to ensure successful coordination\nfor all media events.",
"words": [
